---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqSchema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you actually do the work, or just consult?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "I consult. I research, recommend, and help you think through the decision. If the recommendation needs execution, that work gets scoped separately through Web Management, Implementation, or another written scope."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What do I have to commit to?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The first step is a fixed diagnostic. After that, ongoing consulting only continues if the shape makes sense. I do not want advisory work floating around without a clear question to answer."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do you measure success?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We measure the thing the decision is about. Sometimes that is search visibility. Sometimes it is positioning clarity, vendor fit, internal capacity, or whether the next move is now obvious enough to act on."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you work with my existing vendors?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. That is often the point. I can help you decide what to ask from an SEO vendor, content person, developer, designer, ad vendor, or internal hire. If the vendor is not the problem, I will not make them the problem."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is this different from hiring a marketing agency?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Agencies usually sell execution. Strategy Consulting sells judgment. You are paying for an outside read on what to do, what to stop doing, and what should be built, hired, delegated, or ignored."
      }
    }
  ]
});
---

<Base title="Strategy Consulting | Marketing-Fluent Advisory" description="Marketing-fluent advisory for visibility, positioning, search, operations, vendors, hiring, and growth decisions." ogImage="/og/services/marketing-strategy.png" ogImageAlt="Strategy Consulting: marketing-fluent advisory.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqSchema} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://codyasmith.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Services","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Strategy Consulting","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services/marketing-strategy"}]})} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Strategy Consulting",
    "url": "https://codyasmith.com/services/marketing-strategy",
    "provider": { "@id": "https://codyasmith.com/#organization" },
    "serviceType": "Strategy Consulting",
    "areaServed": { "@type": "Country", "name": "United States" },
    "description": "Marketing-fluent advisory for visibility, positioning, search, operations, vendors, hiring, and growth decisions. Advice only; execution is scoped separately.",
    "termsOfService": "Advice and recommendations only. Execution is scoped separately before work begins."
  })} />
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative pt-40 pb-24 px-6 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-1/4 w-[600px] h-[400px] bg-amber-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/services" class="reveal inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-neutral-500 text-sm hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors duration-300 mb-8 group">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M7 16l-4-4m0 0l4-4m-4 4h18" />
        </svg>
        All services
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
        <span class="reveal text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em]">02</span>
        <div class="reveal gradient-divider flex-1"></div>
      </div>
      <h1 class="reveal font-serif text-5xl md:text-7xl text-neutral-100 leading-[1.05] mb-6">
        Strategy Consulting
      </h1>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-500 italic text-sm tracking-wide mb-10">Marketing-fluent advisory for decisions that need an outside read.</p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" data-frame="default">
        Sometimes the problem is marketing. Sometimes it only looks like marketing from the outside. Visibility, positioning, search, operations, vendors, hiring, and growth all touch each other. I help you read the whole shape before you commit the business to the next move.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
        Your business has momentum. The question is where to put attention next. Search, content, brand, operations, vendors, hiring, systems: there may be opportunity in all of it, but you cannot do everything at once. I help you choose the next right move.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
        You have conflicting advice, old analytics, vendor opinions, internal pressure, and a list of things someone said you "should" do. I sort through it, name the real decision, and tell you what I would do first.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What this is / isn't -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Clarity</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">What this is and what it isn't.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-8">
          <p class="text-amber-400 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-6">What you get</p>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-neutral-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              A clear read on the decision in front of you
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Market, search, and competitor context
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Recommendations your team can actually act on
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Calls or memos tied to the question at hand
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Plain-language reads on the numbers that matter
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Someone telling you what to stop doing
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-8">
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-6">What I don't do</p>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Run your social media
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Manage your ad campaigns
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Produce your content at scale
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Pretend advice is execution
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Give you vague advice you can't act on
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Quietly absorb scope until nobody knows what was bought
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 dot-grid">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Process</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">Here's how it works.</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" data-vibe="default">
          I start with the actual question, read the context around it, and turn the mess into a recommendation you can act on.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-vibe="beach">
          First I name the gap: visibility, positioning, internal capacity, vendor confusion, or a decision that has been sitting too long. Then I show you what I would do next.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-vibe="mountain">
          I read the system before recommending changes to it: search, site, brand, team, vendors, operations, and whatever else is creating drag around the decision.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative">
        <div class="absolute left-6 md:left-8 top-0 bottom-0 w-px bg-gradient-to-b from-amber-500/40 via-amber-500/20 to-transparent"></div>

        <div class="space-y-16">
          <div class="reveal relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">1</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">I read everything.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">
              Your site, your competitors, your search results, your current tools, your team shape, and the story your market is already hearing. I pull the evidence, name the gaps, and write down what I see.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">
              Site read, content read, competitive read, search landscape, vendor context, and internal capacity. Every recommendation traces back to the evidence behind it.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">
              I get smart on your space before recommending anything. The diagnostic grounds every move that comes after.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="reveal relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/60 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400/60 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">2</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">The read becomes a recommendation.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">
              Not everything matters equally, and some of the things you have been doing may not matter at all. I name the next move, the reason behind it, and the things I would stop doing for now.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">
              A direction document. What the business is deciding, what context matters, and what to focus on first.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">
              A sequenced priority list. Each item has a reason written next to it. Hand it to anyone and they know what decision comes first.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="reveal relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/40 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400/40 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">3</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">Then we keep the question alive.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">
              I show up with the outside read: what changed, what still matters, what to ignore, and what should be decided next. You own the decision. I keep the thinking sharp.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">
              Each call or memo ends with named decisions: what moves up, what waits, what falls off, and why. The reasoning is written down so the next conversation has a starting point.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">
              We talk on a clear cadence. You leave knowing what to focus on next and why. The plan stays current because the context does.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="reveal relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/20 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400/20 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">4</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">The numbers stay in the room.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-frame="default">
              Search visibility, site data, reputation signal, and whatever numbers relate to the decision. If something does not support the recommendation, I say so plainly.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
              The useful numbers go on the table. What changed, what stayed stuck, what is getting clearer, and where the next bet belongs.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
              What did not move. What got noisier. What got clearer. The list of things to drop, rework, or leave alone.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Deliverables -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Deliverables</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">What you walk away with.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 reveal-stagger">
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:0">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Decision map</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">The question, the constraints, the evidence, the tradeoffs, and the next move written in one place.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">A clear map of what the business is actually deciding and what should happen first.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Decision, evidence, options, risks, exclusions, next action. Written so the team can use it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:1">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Competitive read</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">Who your market is comparing you against, what they are saying, and where your position is unclear.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">A clear picture of the market around you and where your business can sound more like itself.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Named competitors, visible claims, search posture, message gaps, and the strategic implication.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:2">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Search and content direction</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">What the website should explain, what content is missing, and what questions your market is already asking.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">Search themes, intent, page gaps, structural recommendations, and the questions a writer or builder needs answered before execution.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">The content direction without pretending consulting is content production.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:3">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Positioning notes</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">Where the business sounds clear, where it sounds generic, and what language should carry more weight.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">Message hierarchy, audience assumptions, claim strength, and the places the site or sales story needs sharper language.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">The language that makes the business easier to understand.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:4">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Strategy memos</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">When something needs your attention, you get a clear memo with the read, the implication, and the recommendation.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">Memos function as strategic pulses between calls. The trigger is named, the context is summarized, and the recommended response is clear.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">When something matters, you hear about it before it turns into background noise.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal glow-card p-6" style="--i:5">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Readouts</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Plain-language readouts on the numbers and context tied to the decision. Written for decision-makers, not analysts.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Portal block: where the strategic engagement lives -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-12 text-center">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">The portal</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">The receipt for the engagement.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal glow-card p-8 md:p-10">
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg" data-frame="default">
          Every engagement runs through one portal: contracts, change orders, invoices, files, milestones, approvals, notifications. One log-in, one source of truth, one place to find anything I've ever done for you.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
          Strategy you can watch happen. Each audit finding traces forward to the recommendation, the brief, the call decision, what got built or dropped. The portal is the engagement made visible.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
          The portal is the audit trail of the strategic engagement. Every recommendation logged, every decision dated, every brief tied to the call it came out of. Nothing the strategy work produces gets forgotten or argued about.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-white/5" style="display:none" data-vibe="mountain">
          Password sign-in with bcrypt hashing. Sessions stored as SHA-256 hashes. Files in encrypted storage with signed time-bound download links. Activity log behind every action. Your data stays yours, end to end.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Mid-page CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center reveal">
      <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-4">Need an outside read?</p>
      <a href="/contact?interest=strategy-consulting" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 border border-white/10 text-neutral-300 font-medium text-sm rounded-lg hover:border-amber-500/25 hover:text-amber-400 transition-all duration-300">
        Let's talk strategy
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Questions</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">Things people ask.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 reveal-stagger">
        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:0">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            Do you actually do the work, or just consult?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            I consult. I research, recommend, and help you think through the decision. If the recommendation needs execution, that work gets scoped separately through Web Management, Implementation, or another written scope.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:1">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            What do I have to commit to?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            The first step is a fixed diagnostic. After that, ongoing consulting only continues if the shape makes sense. I do not want advisory work floating around without a clear question to answer.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:2">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            How do you measure success?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            We measure the thing the decision is about. Sometimes that is search visibility. Sometimes it is positioning clarity, vendor fit, internal capacity, or whether the next move is now obvious enough to act on.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:3">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            Can you work with my existing vendors?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Yes. That is often the point. I can help you decide what to ask from an SEO vendor, content person, developer, designer, ad vendor, or internal hire. If the vendor is not the problem, I will not make them the problem.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:4">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            How is this different from hiring a marketing agency?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Agencies usually sell execution. Strategy Consulting sells judgment. You are paying for an outside read on what to do, what to stop doing, and what should be built, hired, delegated, or ignored.
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Scope -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Scope</p>
